  "term": "localization of function",
  "definition": "Localization of function is the view that different parts of the cerebral hemispheres are specialized for different mental or sensory-motor activities. In this context, it means that functions such as movement, sight, hearing, touch, smell, taste, and certain language disturbances were linked to particular brain centres.",
